   "source": [
    "# 38. What cross-validation technique would you use on a time series data set"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "0ca252b8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Best Cross-Validation Technique for Time Series Data\n",
    "\n",
    "For time series datasets, we generally use:\n",
    "\n",
    "🔥 Time Series Cross-Validation / Forward Chaining\n",
    "\n",
    "(also called Rolling Window Validation)\n",
    "\n",
    "❌ Why Normal Cross-Validation is Wrong?\n",
    "\n",
    "Standard k-fold cross-validation:\n",
    "\n",
    "Randomly shuffles data\n",
    "Causes future data leakage into past\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 This violates the temporal order of time series data.\n",
    "\n",
    "✅ Correct Approach: Train on Past → Test on Future\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "Fold\tTrain\tTest\n",
    "1\tJan–Mar\tApr\n",
    "2\tJan–Apr\tMay\n",
    "3\tJan–May\tJun\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 Training window grows over time.\n",
    "\n",
    "📊 Visualization\n",
    "Fold 1:\n",
    "Train: [Jan Feb Mar]\n",
    "Test : [Apr]\n",
    "\n",
    "Fold 2:\n",
    "Train: [Jan Feb Mar Apr]\n",
    "Test : [May]\n",
    "\n",
    "Fold 3:\n",
    "Train: [Jan Feb Mar Apr May]\n",
    "Test : [Jun]\n",
    "🎯 Why This Works\n",
    "\n",
    "✔️ Respects chronological order\n",
    "✔️ Prevents future leakage\n",
    "✔️ Simulates real-world forecasting\n",
    "\n",
    "✅ Common Time Series CV Techniques\n",
    "🔹 1. Expanding Window (Most Common)\n",
    "Training set keeps growing\n",
    "🔹 2. Rolling Window\n",
    "Fixed-size moving window\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Train: Jan–Mar → Test: Apr\n",
    "Train: Feb–Apr → Test: May\n",
    "\n",
    "✔️ Useful when old data becomes less relevant\n",
    "\n",
    "🚀 In Python (Scikit-learn)\n",
    "\n",
    "Using Scikit-learn:\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import TimeSeriesSplit\n",
    "\n",
    "tscv = TimeSeriesSplit(n_splits=5)\n",
    "\n",
    "for train_index, test_index in tscv.split(X):\n",
    "    print(train_index, test_index)\n",
    "⚠️ Important Interview Point\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 Never shuffle time series data before splitting.\n",
    "\n",
    "🎯 Interview-Ready Answer (Perfect)**\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 “For time series datasets, I would use Time Series Cross-Validation such as forward chaining or rolling window validation. Unlike standard k-fold cross-validation, it preserves chronological order and prevents future data leakage by always training on past data and testing on future data.”\n",
    "\n",
    "🔥 Pro Tip\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 Say this to impress interviewer:\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 “Time series validation should mimic real-world forecasting conditions.”"
   ]
  },
